### =====================================================
### Phase 3 - Epic 2.4: Address Management - API Tests
### =====================================================

### 0. Register a test user for address testing
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Address",
    "lastName": "Tester",
    "email": "address-tester@example.com",
    "password": "AddressTest@123"
}

### 1. Login as address tester
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "address-tester@example.com",
    "password": "AddressTest@123"
}

### 2. Add first address (should be set as default automatically)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzM4NCJ9.eyJyb2xlcyI6WyJDVVNUT01FUiJdLCJ0b2tlblR5cGUiOiJhY2Nlc3MiLCJ1c2VySWQiOiJYWFhYWFhYWCIsInN1YiI6ImFkZHJlc3MtdGVzdGVyQGV4YW1wbGUuY29tIiwiaWF0IjoxNzcxNjA0NzYyLCJleHAiOjE3NzE2MDU2NjJ9.XXX
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "street": "123 Main Street",
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "zipCode": "10001",
    "country": "USA",
    "isDefault": true
}

### 3. Add second address (not default)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "street": "456 Oak Avenue",
    "city": "Los Angeles",
    "state": "CA",
    "zipCode": "90001",
    "country": "USA",
    "isDefault": false
}

### 4. Add third address (not default)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "street": "789 Pine Road",
    "city": "Chicago",
    "state": "IL",
    "zipCode": "60601",
    "country": "USA",
    "isDefault": false
}

### 5. Get all addresses for the user
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Accept: application/json

### 6. Set second address as default
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/<ADDRESS_ID_2>/default
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Content-Type: application/json

### 7. Verify default address changed
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Accept: application/json

### 8. Delete an address (non-default)
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/<ADDRESS_ID_3>
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>

### 9. Verify address was deleted
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Accept: application/json

### 10. Delete default address (system should set another as default)
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/<ADDRESS_ID_2>
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>

### 11. Verify new default address was set
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Accept: application/json

### 12. Try to access addresses of another user (should fail with 403 or 404)
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/<ANOTHER_USER_ADDRESS_ID>
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>

### 13. Add address with validation error (missing required field)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "zipCode": "10001",
    "country": "USA"
}

### 14. Add address with empty street field
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer <TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "street": "",
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "zipCode": "10001",
    "country": "USA"
}

### =====================================================
### Security Tests - Unauthenticated Access
### =====================================================

### S1. Try to add address without authentication
POST http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "street": "123 Main Street",
    "city": "New York",
    "state": "NY",
    "zipCode": "10001",
    "country": "USA"
}

### S2. Try to get addresses without authentication
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses
Accept: application/json

### S3. Try to set default address without authentication
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/some-id/default

### S4. Try to delete address without authentication
DELETE http://localhost:3001/api/users/me/addresses/some-id

